Build and run
-------------

Requires CMake 3.24+, a C17 compiler, and a build tool supported by CMake
(for example Make or Ninja).

  cmake -S . -B build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug
  cmake --build build --parallel
  cmake --build build --target run

For a release build, use a separate build directory:

  cmake -S . -B build-release -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release
  cmake --build build-release --parallel

With a multi-configuration generator, pass --config Debug or --config Release
when building or running. To clean compiled outputs:

  cmake --build build --target clean

To install the application:

  cmake --install build-release --prefix ~/.local

CMake downloads the pinned raylib 6.2 source archive on first configuration,
verifies its SHA-256, and builds it as a static library. Internet access is
needed for that initial download; the source is cached under build/_deps.
No system raylib installation is required. Platform graphics, windowing,
and audio dependencies are still required. On macOS install Xcode command-line
tools. Linux dependency instructions:
https://github.com/raysan5/raylib/wiki/Working-on-GNU-Linux

The generated compilation database in build/ is used by clangd with Make or
Ninja generators.

